{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PVVxjfCFKCBdP3F32cRyC7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd089-chmod\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/chmod: Change File Mode Bits\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships a BSD chmod that differs from GNU chmod in recursive behavior, verbose\n6\t  output, and symbolic mode parsing edge cases. The Go implementation must match the\n7\t  Homebrew GNU reference binary (gchmod, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all\n8\t  flag combinations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Change file permission bits using octal or symbolic mode specifications.\n12\t  - G2: Support recursive mode changes with -R.\n13\t  - G3: Support verbose, changes-only, and silent output modes.\n14\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against gchmod via differential testing.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: Mode specification\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: Must accept an octal mode (e.g., 755, 0644) and set the file's permission bits to that value.\n22\t      - R1.2:\n23\t          text: \"Must accept symbolic mode specifications: [ugoa][+-=][rwxXst] with comma-separated clauses (e.g., u+x, go-w, a=rw). Must support multiple comma-separated clauses (e.g., u=rwx,go=rx).\"\n24\t      - R1.3:\n25\t          text: Must process multiple FILE arguments, applying the mode change to each.\n26\t      - R1.4:\n27\t          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be accessed, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n28\t\n29\t  R2:\n30\t    title: Recursive and output control\n31\t    items:\n32\t      - R2.1:\n33\t          text: \"-R or --recursive must change modes recursively for directories and their contents.\"\n34\t      - R2.2:\n35\t          text: \"-v or --verbose must print a diagnostic for every file processed.\"\n36\t      - R2.3:\n37\t          text: \"-c or --changes must print a diagnostic only for files whose mode actually changed.\"\n38\t      - R2.4:\n39\t          text: \"-f or --silent or --quiet must suppress most error messages.\"\n40\t\n41\t  R3:\n42\t    title: Special mode bits and reference\n43\t    items:\n44\t      - R3.1:\n45\t          text: \"Must support setuid (u+s), setgid (g+s), and sticky bit (o+t) in symbolic mode.\"\n46\t      - R3.2:\n47\t          text: \"--reference=RFILE must set each FILE's mode to match RFILE's mode.\"\n48\t\n49\t  R4:\n50\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n51\t    items:\n52\t      - R4.1:\n53\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully.\n54\t      - R4.2:\n55\t          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be accessed or the mode specification is invalid.\n56\t      - R4.3:\n57\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n58\t\n59\tnon_goals:\n60\t  - cmd/chmod does not implement SELinux context changes.\n61\t  - cmd/chmod does not implement --preserve-root (not applicable on macOS).\n62\t\n63\tacceptance_criteria:\n64\t  - id: AC1\n65\t    criterion: \"chmod 755 file sets permissions to rwxr-xr-x, matching gchmod.\"\n66\t    traces:\n67\t      - R1.1\n68\t      - R1.3\n69\t  - id: AC2\n70\t    criterion: \"chmod u+x,go-w file applies symbolic mode correctly, matching gchmod.\"\n71\t    traces:\n72\t      - R1.2\n73\t  - id: AC3\n74\t    criterion: \"chmod -R 644 dir recursively changes all files, matching gchmod -R.\"\n75\t    traces:\n76\t      - R2.1\n77\t  - id: AC4\n78\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gchmod passes for all required test cases.\"\n79\t    traces:\n80\t      - R1.1\n81\t      - R1.2\n82\t      - R2.1\n83\t  - id: AC5\n84\t    criterion: \"cmd/chmod compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n85\t    traces:\n86\t      - R1.1\n87\t      - R1.2\n88\t      - R1.3\n89\t      - R1.4\n90\t      - R2.1\n91\t      - R2.2\n92\t      - R2.3\n93\t      - R2.4\n94\t      - R3.1\n95\t      - R3.2\n96\t      - R4.1\n97\t      - R4.2\n98\t      - R4.3\n99\t\n100\tpackage_contract:\n101\t  imports:\n102\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n103\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e85d7acb-a15f-4453-9edb-f79e3459e60b","uuid":"f012c6c3-2280-49cf-a569-23d3a6fc9805","timestamp":"2026-05-23T17:09:53.047Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5548/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd089-chmod.yaml","content":"id: srd089-chmod\ntitle: \"cmd/chmod: Change File Mode Bits\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships a BSD chmod that differs from GNU chmod in recursive behavior, verbose\n  output, and symbolic mode parsing edge cases. The Go implementation must match the\n  Homebrew GNU reference binary (gchmod, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all\n  flag combinations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Change file permission bits using octal or symbolic mode specifications.\n  - G2: Support recursive mode changes with -R.\n  - G3: Support verbose, changes-only, and silent output modes.\n  - G4: Verify functional parity against gchmod via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Mode specification\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must accept an octal mode (e.g., 755, 0644) and set the file's permission bits to that value.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"Must accept symbolic mode specifications: [ugoa][+-=][rwxXst] with comma-separated clauses (e.g., u+x, go-w, a=rw). Must support multiple comma-separated clauses (e.g., u=rwx,go=rx).\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must process multiple FILE arguments, applying the mode change to each.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be accessed, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Recursive and output control\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-R or --recursive must change modes recursively for directories and their contents.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-v or --verbose must print a diagnostic for every file processed.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"-c or --changes must print a diagnostic only for files whose mode actually changed.\"\n      - R2.4:\n          text: \"-f or --silent or --quiet must suppress most error messages.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Special mode bits and reference\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"Must support setuid (u+s), setgid (g+s), and sticky bit (o+t) in symbolic mode.\"\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"--reference=RFILE must set each FILE's mode to match RFILE's mode.\"\n\n  R4:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be accessed or the mode specification is invalid.\n      - R4.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/chmod does not implement SELinux context changes.\n  - cmd/chmod does not implement --preserve-root (not applicable on macOS).\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"chmod 755 file sets permissions to rwxr-xr-x, matching gchmod.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"chmod u+x,go-w file applies symbolic mode correctly, matching gchmod.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"chmod -R 644 dir recursively changes all files, matching gchmod -R.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gchmod passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"cmd/chmod compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":103,"startLine":1,"totalLines":103}}}
